{
  "schemaVersion": "atm.workItem.v0.2",
  "workItemId": "ATM-GOV-0366",
  "title": "Disclose the owner-lane source in lane capability refusals",
  "status": "done",
  "milestone": null,
  "dependencies": [],
  "acceptance": [
    "ACC-1 A blocked attempt reports the ledger record that decided it and a `nextCommand` that reads that record, with no task, actor or path special cases in the control flow.",
    "ACC-2 No refusal payload contains the owner lane id or the claim's export hint, whatever actor string the attempt presents. It reports only that the hint exists and where to read it.",
    "ACC-3 The gate is unchanged: every previously blocked attempt is still blocked, and the existing hard-gate regressions still pass.",
    "ACC-4 The disclosure is derived from the same claim read that produces the decision and is carried on the decision, so no consumer re-reads the ledger to describe a decision it did not make (INV-ATM-012)."
  ],
  "deliverables": [
    "packages/cli/src/commands/lane-session/capability-authority.ts",
